WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
In Users, choose Add User. We will prepare an invitation

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.200
for Taylor Brooks using a fictional email address.

00:00:07.917 --> 00:00:12.107
Enter the teammate’s first name, last name, and email. Check

00:00:12.107 --> 00:00:16.298
the spelling before continuing; the invitation is associated with this

00:00:16.298 --> 00:00:16.717
address.

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:21.881
Choose Agent. The form now shows Sales Channel, Work Location,

00:00:21.881 --> 00:00:23.667
NPN, and Employment Type.

00:00:24.458 --> 00:00:29.664
Review Telesales, select Remote, and enter the agent’s NPN. Check

00:00:29.664 --> 00:00:33.308
Employment Type; this example uses a contractor.

00:00:34.008 --> 00:00:37.851
Choose Add User to create the invitation. Taylor appears as

00:00:37.851 --> 00:00:40.158
Pending while account setup is unfinished.

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:47.851
Now open Priya Shah, an existing active agent. This is

00:00:47.851 --> 00:00:52.209
a separate profile demonstration. Taylor’s new invitation remains pending.

00:00:52.925 --> 00:00:57.643
Under Details, review Employment: role, Training, sales channel, work location,

00:00:57.643 --> 00:01:02.360
and employment type. Training provides listen-only learning access when the

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:03.775
dialer is enabled.

00:01:04.508 --> 00:01:08.243
Open Licensed States to review states for each product. Use

00:01:08.243 --> 00:01:10.858
the agent’s main agency when making changes.

00:01:11.558 --> 00:01:15.752
Open Contracts to review this existing agent’s carriers and relationships.

00:01:15.752 --> 00:01:19.108
Verify these details before the agent starts selling.

00:01:19.808 --> 00:01:24.391
In Marketplace, open Manage Access for the relevant queue. Review

00:01:24.391 --> 00:01:28.058
agent eligibility and intended access before making assignments.
